{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":141726,"duration_api_ms":209558,"num_turns":11,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ded0f704-8c44-4366-8525-b027721d4d99","total_cost_usd":0.6948153000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31219,"cache_read_input_tokens":199191,"output_tokens":3459,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31219,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":191,"outputTokens":11831,"cacheReadInputTokens":1534463,"cacheCreationInputTokens":80639,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3135910499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":3459,"cacheReadInputTokens":199191,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31219,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.38122425,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all four amendments against source code. Two are real defects (double feeding rate, save migration regression), one is an enhancement request not a correctness issue, and one is based on a factually incorrect premise (the test already exists).","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-6b4f7f03","decision":"reject","rationale":"Confirmed TankSnapshot omits reserve_g and daily_food_consumed_g, but the budget ledger already exposes animal.reserve_g in diagnostics. This is a UI/API surface enhancement, not a correctness or safety defect. Additionally, daily_food_consumed_g is reset at the end of the daily shrimp step, so it would show 0 in most snapshot timings, making it misleading rather than helpful."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-d8db9c4a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in shrimp.rs: both periphyton demand (line 140) and detritus demand (line 149) are computed as `total_feeding_units * rate * grazing_access_factor` independently. When both pools are available, total intake reaches 2x the configured shrimp_periphyton_grazing_g_per_shrimp_per_day parameter. This is semantically surprising given the parameter name implies a total grazing cap, and it inflates bioload, waste, and O2 demand beyond what parameterization suggests. Either documenting the intentional double-feeding or splitting the budget is a warranted fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-1858fe11","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's central claim is factually wrong. The test `oxygen_limited_respiration_scales_dissolved_fluxes_and_retains_shortfall` exists at shrimp.rs:830 and directly exercises this path: it sets DO to 10.0 mg (below full O2 demand), calls route_consumed_food, and asserts (1) DO floors at 0.0, (2) DIC is scaled by respiration_scale, (3) TAN and alkalinity scale with the same factor, and (4) reserve captures the growth fraction plus unrespired shortfall. All four verification points from the amendment are already covered."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-ec3b52d2","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: migrate_v3_to_v4 is a no-op (save.rs:323-329), reserve_g defaults to 0.0 via serde(default), and both fund_hatched_clutch_biomass and fund_live_shrimp_biomass hard-check reserve_g before proceeding. A v3 save with berried females needs ~0.25g reserve per clutch hatch (25 juveniles × 0.05g × 0.20), and juvenile maturation needs ~0.014g per candidate — both impossible with reserve_g=0. This silently breaks reproduction for any upgraded v3 save with in-flight breeding. The test at save_load.rs:274-320 codifies this regression rather than fixing it. A migration that seeds reserve from existing colony state (or at minimum provides enough reserve to honor in-progress egg/maturation commitments) is needed."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"de04a162-44fc-4d0c-b8e6-719fd180ed6c"}
